oker service in Altinn 3 [1]\n\nA policy consists of one to many rules, and each rule is made up of three distinct parts [1]:\n- **Resources** – Describes the resource(s) a rule applies to (e.g., an app, a resource in the resource register, a specific task, or any other sub-resources). A single rule can combine multiple resources [1].\n- **Action** – Describes which action(s) the rules apply to (e.g., read, write, sign, fire, Opendoor +++). A single rule can target mul…", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-authz-05-xacml-policy-regelstruktur", :empty? false, :llm-calls 2, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 341, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-authorization,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d9ed057e7daaa R— P4.8 h4.0 or1.9 L3881 1/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+metadata+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.5,0.1,0.0] +q | Xacml", :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "c28fc018e0d0;64e0accf6d5c", :enrichment-hits 23, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 1, :prompt-tokens 5070, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "c28fc018e0d0", :expected-chunk-ids "c28fc018e0d0", :elapsed-ms 356353, :issued-queries "XACML policy description | XACML rule structure components parts | what is a XACML policy Altinn", :timestamp "2026-06-10T12:09:22.504029Z", :total-tokens 5411, :run-id "75d15e95-2f8e-4a08-a726-2daa37158d62", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response "Based on the provided context:\n\n- **Default value:** The required authentication level is set to `2` by default [1].\n- **How to configure it in XACML:** You define this using the obligation part of the XACML Policy file [1]. Specifically, you add an `<xacml:ObligationExpression>` inside `<xacml:ObligationExpressions>`, and assign your desired integer value to the attribute with `Category=\"urn:altinn:minimum-authenticationlevel\"` within a `<xacml:AttributeValue DataType=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer\">` element [1]. \n\n**Important scope distinction for higher levels:** If you set the main required authentication level to `4`, you must also explicitly define a separate obligation for service owners using `Category=\"urn:altinn:minimum-authenticationlevel-org\"` and set its value to `…", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-authz-06-xacml-obligation-authlevel", :empty? false, :llm-calls 2, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 484, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-authorization,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d0453a21f0b21 R25.1 P3.6 h3.0 or2.0 L1853 4/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Authorization", :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 3, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "e246b621f86c;7edbd10a3604;fe6b6b04a08b", :enrichment-hits 42, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 6385, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "e246b621f86c;fe6b6b04a08b", :expected-chunk-ids "e246b621f86c", :elapsed-ms 386523, :issued-queries "authentication level XACML policy | set required authentication level access control | XACML AuthenticationLevel configuration | default authentication level XACML", :timestamp "2026-06-10T12:15:49.031321Z", :total-tokens 6869, :run-id "179ea805-9621-4817-a08d-3bb8d1df0d0d", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, Altinn Authorization supports four explicitly defined user types: **Users**, **Organization**, **Service owner**, and **System user** [1]. \n\nRegarding their ability to submit or act on behalf of a party in an app, the sources draw clear distinctions using specific terminology:\n\n*   **Users**: Authenticated via ID-porten (or Altinn Portal), these are standard end-users with a User ID, Party ID, and profile. They **can represent other parties through party selection** [1]. From the app's perspective, this follows a normal user-driven flow where authenticated end-users handle submissions [3].\n*   **Organization**: The documentation explicitly states that organizations **\"are not valid submitters\"** because an organization cannot submit on behalf of itself within…", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-authz-07-bruker-typer-authorization", :empty? false, :llm-calls 2, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 305, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-authorization,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d8f46ae005cbe R23.8 P3.6 h3.0 or2.0 L2463 1/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Auth", :source "new", :search-passes 2, :n-retrieved 3, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "8d82f06ea710;e91ae6feb41d;d7788a9552f1", :enrichment-hits 79, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? false, :n-cited 3, :prompt-tokens 6305, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "8d82f06ea710;e91ae6feb41d;d7788a